{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq '.grounding_sources | type, (if type==\\\"array\\\" then .[0:3] else to_entries[0:3] end)' paper_data.json; jq '.evidence_sources | type, (if type==\\\"array\\\" then .[0:2] else to_entries[0:2] end)' paper_data.json; jq '.final_evaluation | {status,outcome,correct,metrics,evaluation_evidence:(.evaluation_evidence|keys)}' paper_data.json; jq '.supplementary_plan.planned_subsections[5],.central_thesis,.edit_framing_decision' paper_strategy.json; sed -n '120,145p' paper_strategy.md; find / -name apply_patch -type f 2>/dev/null | head; rg --files .codex | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq '.grounding_sources | type, (if type==\\\"array\\\" then .[0:3] else to_entries[0:3] end)' paper_data.json; jq '.evidence_sources | type, (if type==\\\"array\\\" then .[0:2] else to_entries[0:2] end)' paper_data.json; jq '.final_evaluation | {status,outcome,correct,metrics,evaluation_evidence:(.evaluation_evidence|keys)}' paper_data.json; jq '.supplementary_plan.planned_subsections[5],.central_thesis,.edit_framing_decision' paper_strategy.json; sed -n '120,145p' paper_strategy.md; find / -name apply_patch -type f 2>/dev/null | head; rg --files .codex | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"\"object\"\n[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\": \"unverified\",\n      \"episode_count\": 3,\n      \"evaluation_scope\": \"sealed_final\",\n      \"id\": \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n      \"json_pointer\": \"/episodes\",\n      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261112_215151/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n      \"path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261112_215151/final_evaluation/results/evaluation_evidence.json\",\n      \"program_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:d566dbc8e195fa324a33bf02f2c26e6c662797861c770832e9b4e90da2f9a48e\",\n      \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:96ab9e596f643b15a4319c2645a84a5817f462267d84a3ce84c1a61b04817fea\",\n      \"sha256\": \"sha256:b7221c00e990439249bd5eaa9ba7e05598ec0a91d28a9abd2d6ac0529aa32981\",\n      \"type\": \"evaluation_evidence\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"key\": \"final.metric.candidate_mae\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"evaluation_scope\": \"sealed_final\",\n      \"id\": \"final.metric.candidate_mae\",\n      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261112_215151/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n      \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:96ab9e596f643b15a4319c2645a84a5817f462267d84a3ce84c1a61b04817fea\",\n      \"type\": \"metric\",\n      \"value\": 0.031296949105441715\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"key\": \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"evaluation_scope\": \"sealed_final\",\n      \"id\": \"final.metric.combined_score\",\n      \"manifest_path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261112_215151/final_evaluation/final_manifest.json\",\n      \"results_tree_sha256\": \"sha256:96ab9e596f643b15a4319c2645a84a5817f462267d84a3ce84c1a61b04817fea\",\n      \"type\": \"metric\",\n      \"value\": 0.9687030508945583\n    }\n  }\n]\n\"object\"\n[\n  {\n    \"key\": \"ablations\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261112_215151/ablations\",\n      \"status\": \"missing\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"key\": \"investigation\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261112_215151/investigation\",\n      \"status\": \"included\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"outcome\": \"qualified\",\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"candidate_mae\": 0.031296949105441715,\n    \"combined_score\": 0.9687030508945583,\n    \"correct\": 1,\n    \"greedy_ridge_mae\": 0.036070484115358764,\n    \"historical_mean_mae\": 0.08782454238980078,\n    \"observed_copy_mae\": 0.23263708759651222,\n    \"permutation_gap\": 0.05846745542827772,\n    \"permuted_mae\": 0.08976440453371944,\n    \"random_lowrank_mae\": 0.04563401706946738\n  },\n  \"evaluation_evidence\": [\n    \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\",\n    \"episode_count\",\n    \"episodes\",\n    \"path\",\n    \"sha256\",\n    \"status\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"heading\": \"LLM Usage\",\n  \"grounded_content\": \"Disclose the documented roles of automated agents in idea generation, implementation, reference-query planning, and paper framing, and disclose later writing/figure assistance only if it actually occurs. Do not invent human verification, external reading, experiments, or a model identity absent from the logs.\",\n  \"source_ids\": [],\n  \"source_paths\": [\n    \"global_memory/memory.jsonl\",\n    \"memory.md\",\n    \"reference_query_plan.md\",\n    \"paper_strategy.md\"\n  ]\n}\n\"On the evaluated English MTEB panels, the frozen latent-model procedure has lower aggregate prediction error than the evaluated random-acquisition low-rank and greedy-coverage ridge pipelines, including on never-queryable audit targets, but the advantage is not uniform across held-out splits and does not isolate the contribution of mixtures or value-adaptive acquisition.\"\n\"Not an edit-mode run: previous_paper, staged new/old programs, aggregated, extra_tasks, contributions.md, and instantiated edit-context files are absent. Rejected means no inherited manuscript story is adopted, not that an existing manuscript was evaluated and rejected. Preserve-the-prior-story is inapplicable; broadening the source brief to generative language models is unsupported; recentering on the latest quadrature branch is unsupported. Select the frozen evaluated latent-model family, with the two split conditions as evidence blocks under one thesis.\"\n## Supplementary Information After References\n\nThe supplement adds auditable depth, not a hiding place for central negative evidence:\n\n1. **Complete Budget-Resolved Prediction Errors.** All recorded checkpoints, split seeds, conditions, original/permuted arms, evaluated pipelines, historical means, and queried-score averages, for both error definitions. Exclude replay from averages. Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes` and the corresponding final metric IDs.\n2. **Aggregation and Common-Target Comparisons.** Exact weights, seed-level paired deltas, and policy-specific versus unchanged-target views. Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes`; implementation: `task/evaluate_final.py`.\n3. **Observed-Data Inference and Historical Model Choice.** Faithful EM/conditioning equations, implemented candidate grids, regularization, bounded median, transfer heuristics, historical-only fixed-target validation, and fallback. The source’s `max(0.0001, 0.5 paired SE)` margin is a selection heuristic, not a significance test. Grounding is the selected `src/covariance.py`, `src/mixture.py`, and `src/METHOD.md`, not unverified internal performance. These files lack catalogued paper-data source IDs; use explicit paths rather than inventing IDs.\n4. **Frozen Data, Score Contexts, and Reproduction.** Pinned source revision, normalization, task-context keys, resource checksums, natural missingness, name-proxy families, mask-defined availability, seeds, dependency versions, and existing commands/interface. Sources: frozen resources, task contract, final manifest, `final.evidence.episodes`, and qualification provenance. Separate recorded evaluator timing from unmeasured method-only runtime or actual evaluation-cost savings. Anonymize public paths.\n5. **Permutation and Reset Controls.** Complete recorded control tables and deterministic replay; distinguish protocol checks from predictive evidence. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, permutation metric IDs, and `final.qualification.*`.\n6. **LLM Usage.** Disclose agent roles supported by implementation/status documents and append-only logs; add later drafting/figure assistance only if it occurs. Do not claim human validation, unread literature review, unrun experiments, or an undocumented model identity. No fabricated scientific source IDs are needed for this process disclosure.\n\nThe writer may receive a later authoritative analysis ranking; route appendix-ranked material here without retroactively altering this strategy. No absent robustness study or posthoc ranking is presumed complete.\n\n## Limitations That Must Stay Visible\n\n- Only pinned English embedding panels are evaluated, not generative LLMs, multilingual tasks, every upstream model, or every MTEB benchmark.\n- Naturally missing target scores have no ground truth here. Retrospective query availability is supplied from each target row’s recorded mask with audit columns removed. This does not establish prospective availability or arbitrary missing-not-at-random recovery.\n- Name-derived family proxies and frozen-data content checks do not guarantee complete architectural/lineage independence, population-level generalization, or absence of all contamination.\n- Cross-pipeline comparisons do not identify which component helps. Actual mixture choices, acquisition adaptation, fallback frequency, uncertainty calibration, cost-weighted selection, missingness sensitivity, and additional-dataset replication are not externally established.\n- Query count is not measured compute or monetary savings; real benchmarks have unequal costs. No universal sufficient budget or accepted-error threshold is demonstrated.\n- The adverse split, small and dependent split-seed set, target-set dependence, and incomplete mechanism attribution belong in the main discussion even though aggregate errors favor the procedure.\n\n## Literature and Writing Guardrails\n\n`references.bib` and `references_provenance.json` exist. At inspection they contain a retrieved method-oriented pool, including `Ghahramani1996TheEA`; essential MTEB and several explicitly allowed starter titles are not in that pool. Retrieval metadata is not evidence of reading a source’s scientific conclusions. Before final drafting, verify a small relevant subset of permitted original sources and safely retrieve missing explicitly allowed starter works. Avoid broad discovery, citation chasing, and all prohibited work or discussion of it. Do not infer or search for the prohibited paper’s identity. No network retrieval was performed for this strategy.\n\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/openalex_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/scholarly_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/s2_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/alifeconf.sty\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/alife/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/references.bib\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/claims_grounding.schema.json\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n.codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.bst\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.sty\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
